Discovered while fixing karr #6 (Result::Item realignment): once CLI/Cmd/Items.pm no longer crashed on ->category, t/30-cli.t ran further and hit the identical silent-break pattern in Quest and Arc.

CLI/Cmd/Quest.pm calls ->type, ->next_quest, ->prev_quest, ->reputation_reward, ->last_updated -- none exist on Result::Quest (which has id, name, objectives, xp, granted_items, created_at, updated_at, locations, marker_category, image, guide_links, trader_name, sort_order, position, required_items, rewards, _raw).

CLI/Cmd/Arc.pm calls ->type, ->maps, ->duration, ->cooldown, ->xp_reward, ->coin_reward, ->loot, ->last_updated -- Result::Arc only has id, name, description, icon, image, created_at, updated_at.

This was masked until now because the Items.pm crash killed t/30 before reaching those subtests. Needs the same treatment as #6: verify against the live API (https://metaforge.app/api/arc-raiders/quests and /arcs, both free/no-auth) which real fields exist, remap or drop each CLI accessor accordingly, exact-format rule applies (no fabricated fields). t/30-cli.t will not go green without this.

Fixed: CLI/Cmd/Quest.pm and CLI/Cmd/Arc.pm no longer call non-existent Result accessors (type, description on Quest, maps, duration, cooldown, xp_reward, coin_reward, reputation_reward, prev_quest, next_quest, last_updated). Quest.pm: xp_reward->xp, last_updated->updated_at, Type/Description/Rewards-reputation/Quest-Chain blocks removed (Description block was unreachable dead code before since Result::Quest never had that attribute). Arc.pm: Type/Maps/Duration/Cooldown/Rewards(xp/coin) blocks removed, last_updated->updated_at, Loot Drops rendering rewritten for the real nested shape ({item:{name,...}}, no chance field). Result::Arc gained a new 'loot' ArrayRef attribute (default []), populated only when includeLoot=true is passed - CLI/Cmd/Arc.pm's arcs_paginated/arcs_all calls now pass includeLoot=>'true' so the detail view actually gets loot data. POD in both CLI commands updated to match. Verified via 'timeout 25 perl -Ilib -It/lib t/30-cli.t' and t/13-arcraiders-result-arc.t - all green for the touched paths; the pre-existing TODO block in t/30-cli.t for this ticket now passes (quest detail no longer crashes; arc detail no longer crashes, though the fixture's arc name doesn't match the test's search term 'salvage-run' - that's a fixture/test issue for the test-writer, not a lib bug). Only lib/ touched, t/ untouched per instructions.

